# Design Handoff — Waitlist → Product Landing

This repo (`leadgrab-waitlist`) is the **design source of truth** for marketing UI until the product app exists.

## When building the product landing page

1. Read **all files** in `.cursor/rules/product-landing-handoff/` before writing UI code.
2. Clone or reference this repo at tag `design-v1` (or latest `main` if no tag yet).
3. Copy files marked **COPY AS-IS** in `file-manifest.md` first (theme, UI primitives, assets).
4. Copy files marked **ADAPT** and follow `cta-migration.md` + `page-structure.md`.
5. Do **not** copy waitlist-only files (modal, form, API route, Web3Forms/Resend).
6. Keep product copy in the product repo's `lib/copy.ts`, seeded from this repo's `lib/copy.ts`.

## Repo relationship

| Repo | Role |
|------|------|
| `leadgrab-waitlist` (this) | Waitlist validation site — frozen design reference |
| `leadgrab` / `wa-leadgrab` (future) | Product app + extension — receives borrowed UI |

## Stable design snapshot

After visual polish on this waitlist site, tag it:

```bash
git tag design-v1
git push origin design-v1
```

Use that tag when copying into the product repo so both sides match.
